  "narrative": "All returned estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For dependency_composite, a threshold-level finding requires a signed effect above 0.15 composite dependency-score units in the claimed direction with uncertainty consistent with a meaningful effect. H18, H19, H118, and H119 are robustness checks within the dominant adenocarcinoma subtype for the four mature predictors. H18 gives R93 signed +0.760 with interval +0.686 to +0.833, consistent with SMARCA4 loss being associated with stronger measured dependency within adenocarcinoma. H19 gives R94 signed +0.828 with interval +0.753 to +0.902, consistent with TP53 loss being associated with weaker measured dependency. H118 gives R95 signed +0.800 with interval +0.721 to +0.880, consistent with KEAP1 loss being associated with weaker dependency. H119 gives R96 signed +0.740 with interval +0.611 to +0.869, consistent with MSI-high being associated with stronger dependency. These are large, lower-bounds well above threshold, and biologically consistent with the already accepted dataset-specific associations, so all four are accepted and closed. They remain dataset-specific subgroup robustness results, not causal or generalizable claims.\n\nThe high-Cas9 activity interaction tests do not support technical editing efficiency as a meaningful effect modifier of the accepted predictors. H124, SMARCA4 loss interaction in high Cas9 activity, R97 signed -0.058 with interval -0.220 to +0.105, is opposite the claimed amplification direction and small. H125, TP53 loss interaction, R98 signed +0.003 with interval -0.148 to +0.154, is essentially null; although the upper bound just crosses the threshold, the point estimate and lower bound do not support a threshold effect. H126, KEAP1 loss interaction, R99 signed -0.125 with interval -0.289 to +0.040, is opposite direction and below threshold. H127, MSI-high interaction, R100 signed +0.006 with interval -0.260 to +0.272, is null and relies on only 28 exposed high-Cas9 MSI-high samples, providing no support for the claimed context effect. These interaction claims are rejected and closed.\n\nThe upper-half AXL expression interaction tests also do not support amplification of the accepted predictors relative to the lower-AXL complement. H128 gives R101 signed +0.068 with interval -0.057 to +0.194, below threshold and interval-inconsistent with support. H129 gives R102 signed -0.037 with interval -0.160 to +0.086, opposite direction and null. H130 gives R103 signed +0.037 with interval -0.094 to +0.167, below threshold and null. H131 gives R104 signed -0.179 with interval -0.397 to +0.039; although the point magnitude exceeds the threshold, it is in the opposite direction from the registered claim, which was amplification of the MSI-high effect in high AXL. This may be a signal of attenuation of the MSI-high association in high-AXL samples, but it was not the pre-specified claim direction and would require a separate confirmatory hypothesis and validation before being interpreted. Therefore H131 is rejected and closed as an amplification claim, and no post hoc attenuation conclusion is accepted here. No independent validation is requested at this stage because the accepted subgroup robustness results are large and consistent with previously validated main effects, while the interaction results do not provide threshold-level claims in the claimed direction."
